{{Elections in Florida sidebar}}

The '''2022 United States House of Representatives elections in Florida''' were held on November 8, 2022, to elect the 28 [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. representatives]] from [[Florida]], one from each of the state's 28 [[Florida's congressional districts|congressional districts]]. The [[Partisan primary|primary]] was held on August 23, 2022.<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|title=Election Dates - Division of Elections - Florida Department of State |url=https://dos.myflorida.com/elections/for-voters/election-dates/ |access-date=2022-06-28 |website=dos.myflorida.com}}</ref> The elections coincided with the [[2022 United States Senate election in Florida]], [[2022 United States House of Representatives elections|other elections]] to the House of Representatives, [[2022 United States Senate elections|other elections]] to the [[United States Senate]], and various [[2022 United States elections#State elections|state]] and [[2022 United States elections#Local elections|local elections]].

The Republican Party gained four seats, increasing their majority from 16–11 to 20–8. No Republican lost re-election. 
