{{see also|Florida's 6th congressional district}}
Republican [[Michael Waltz]], who had represented the district since 2019, was elected with 60% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0" /> Waltz won re-election in 2022.

The boundaries of the district were redrawn from 2020, determined by the [[2020 United States redistricting cycle|2020 redistricting cycle]]. The 6th district was changed to lose half of Volusia County, while also taking in Putnam County and the eastern portion of Marion County. However, despite experiencing massive changes to his district, and therefore his electorate, Waltz did not face any major primary threats in this election.

