{{see also|Florida's 10th congressional district}}
Democrat [[Val Demings]], who had represented the district since 2017, was re-elected with 63% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0" /> Demings did not run for re-election and instead ran unsuccessfully for the [[2022 United States Senate election in Florida]].

The boundaries of the district were redrawn from 2020, determined by the [[2020 United States redistricting cycle|2020 redistricting cycle]].

