{{see also|Florida's 27th congressional district}}
Republican [[Maria Elvira Salazar]], who had represented the district since 2021, flipped the district and was elected with 51% of the vote in 2020.<ref name=":0" /> Salazar won re-election in 2022.

The boundaries of the district were redrawn from 2020, as determined by the [[2020 United States redistricting cycle|2020 redistricting cycle]]. Miami Beach was removed from the 27th, while the district took in more Cuban-heavy areas inland.

This district was included on the list of Republican-held seats the [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]] was targeting in 2022.<ref name='dccc'/>

